  "published": "2026-06-10T08:03:55.187Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.0 - Major Reliability Release\n\nThis release fixes ~56 verified bugs found in a full-codebase audit and wires up\nseveral previously non-functional features. It contains breaking changes.\n\nNow actually working (previously dead code):\n- Cross-tab sync now APPLIES incoming updates (receive path was never wired)\n- Server sync (SignalR) connects automatically and applies remote updates\n- Plugin lifecycle hooks (OnStoreCreated/OnBeforeUpdate/OnAfterUpdate/OnStoreDisposing)\n- WithHistory(out history) undo/redo on the builder path\n- Redux DevTools ship in the package (runtime-gated: debugger-attached or\n  DevToolsOptions.Enabled = true), including time travel\n- UrlSync ExcludeActions filtering\n- Query client defaults (DefaultStaleTime/DefaultRetry)\n- NEW: RefetchOnWindowFocus / RefetchOnReconnect for queries\n\nBreaking changes:\n- IQueryClient is now scoped (fixes cross-user cache leakage on Blazor Server)\n- Persistence with EnableIntegrityCheck=true (the options-based default) now\n  throws at startup unless a stable SigningKey is supplied\n- Nested UpdateAsync from middleware/updaters throws (previously deadlocked)\n- ActionDispatcher throws on unhandled actions (matches documented contract)\n- AddTransientStore no longer registers reader/writer/observable aliases\n- ServerSync protocol: signed full-state messages, 3-arg JoinDocument\n- TabSync default channel name uses the full type name\n- Store now disposes its middlewares (IAsyncDisposable)\n\nReliability highlights:\n- Fixed cancellation races in Query/Mutation (stale overwrites, duplicate\n  fetches/writes, a process-crash path on Blazor Server)\n- Fixed sensitive-data filter corrupting persisted dictionaries and non-string\n  properties; token-boundary keyword matching (ShippingAddress no longer filtered)\n- Debounced persistence/tab-sync no longer block the store lock and now coalesce\n- Fixed UrlSync wiping state, erasing unrelated query params, and crashing on\n  page-to-page navigation; URL values now merge instead of replace\n- Fixed unbounded memory growth in DiagnosticsService and QueryClient\n- History grouping no longer corrupts the undo stack after Undo\n\nv2.0.12 - Persistence Hydration Fixes (fixes #11)\n\nBug Fixes:\n- WithPersistence(provider, options) and WithSecurePersistence() now hydrate\n  state on init in WebAssembly mode (previously only WithPersistence(sp, key) did)\n- Unified sync hydration path: wrapper format, HMAC signature verification,\n  state validation, and TransformOnLoad are applied consistently across all\n  WithPersistence overloads\n- Hydration errors now log to ILogger and Console.Error (was silent\n  Debug.WriteLine in Release WASM)\n- New public API: PersistenceMiddleware.TryLoadStateSync() for advanced scenarios\n\nv2.0.9 - LLM-Friendly Documentation\n\nNew Features:\n- Added llms.txt and llms-full.txt following llmstxt.org specification\n- Enables AI agents to navigate documentation more effectively\n\nv2.0.8 - AsyncData Refetch Support\n\nNew Features:\n- Added IsFetching property to AsyncData for tracking fetch operations\n- Added IsRefetching computed property (true when refetching while data exists)\n- Added ToLoadingPreserved() method for stale-while-revalidate pattern\n- Preserves existing data during background refetches\n\nv2.0.7 - URL Sync (Experimental)\n\nNew Features:\n- UrlSyncStoreComponent<T> base class for bidirectional URL-state synchronization\n- [AutoSyncWithQuery] attribute for zero-boilerplate query parameter binding\n- Fluent IUrlSyncBuilder API for manual configuration\n- 3-layer circular update prevention\n- Configurable debounce and navigation modes (Replace/Push)\n- Convention-based auto-discovery of URL mappings\n\nv2.0.6 - Cache Invalidation Convenience Methods\n\nNew Features:\n- Added convenience wrapper methods in StoreComponentWithUtilities for cache invalidation:\n  - InvalidateCachedResult(key) - Remove specific cached entry\n  - InvalidateCachedResultsByPrefix(prefix) - Remove entries by prefix\n  - ClearCachedResults() - Clear all cached results\n- Improved discoverability of cache management APIs\n\nv2.0.5 - ExecuteCachedAsync\n- Added ExecuteCachedAsync for deduplicated async actions with caching\n- Deduplicates both fetch AND state updates across concurrent callers\n\nv2.0.4 - Bug Fixes & Stability\n(See previous release notes for full changelog)",
